          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for Binglao poker where both high and low hands are rewarded and ace may be high or low in straights.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Suits are used for flushes; standard poker hand rankings apply. The best high hand and the best qualifying low hand may split the pot in this high-low variant.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit: ace (high or low in straights), king, queen, jack, ten, nine, eight, seven, six, five, four, three, two. Standard poker order for high hands; for low, the best hand is the lowest five cards (e.g. 7-5-4-3-2) with ace counting low.',
